        "q2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will these work for TRREB and Realtor.ca?",
            "answer": "Yes. Files come back at standard dimensions for TRREB and Realtor.ca. We include disclosure wording and recommend noting virtual staging on the listing."
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "It's a 480 sq ft junior one-bedroom. Is staging going to look ridiculous?",
            "answer": "Not if it's done to scale, which is the point. The buyer wants to know whether a real bed and a real sofa fit — furniture that oversizes the room fails that test at the showing, so we furnish honestly."
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does this compare to hiring a Toronto staging company?",
            "answer": "A downtown staging company typically charges for furniture plus a monthly rental period. Virtual staging is {price:virtual-staging} a photo, once, with no rental clock running if the listing takes longer than expected."
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I use the staged images anywhere besides MLS?",
            "answer": "Yes — the staged photos are yours. MLS, a virtual tour, social ads, brochures and print all work, provided the virtual staging is disclosed in each. Many realtors get the most out of a staged photo in paid social, where it is the image that stops the scroll."
          }
        },
        "q6": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Which Toronto properties benefit most from virtual staging?",
            "answer": "Vacant condos first — an empty space gives potential buyers nothing to anchor to. After that: small or awkward layouts where furniture placement proves the room actually works, tenanted units where we remove the existing furniture, pre-construction where there is nothing to photograph yet, and stale listings that need a real reason to relaunch."
          }
        },
